# Filename-pinned baseline for scripts/check-evidence-grounding.sh (gate evidence.grounding).
#
# Every entry below is a point-in-time evidence document whose citations were
# TRUE WHEN WRITTEN and whose subject has since moved. An entry is an exact doc
# path or a directory prefix ending in `/`, and carries its class tag as a
# trailing comment. Enforcement is two-way and shrink-only: a NEW uncovered
# offender fails, and an entry that stops covering any finding fails until it is
# pruned. Pinning the archive silences history, never a citation written today —
# a finding on a line ADDED since BASE_REF is not excused by this file.
#
# Seeded 2026-08-26 from the tree at 8cdcb5a90: 618 findings across 45 keys.
# The classes, and why each is pinned rather than fixed:
#
#   dated-recon-snapshot  A recon/audit run captured the tree on a named date.
#                         Its file inventory IS the record; rewriting the paths
#                         would falsify the snapshot.
#   dated-audit           A dated audit or readiness review of a surface that
#                         has since been refactored or retired.
#   dated-duel            A dated multi-model duel/review corpus, including raw
#                         model transcripts that must stay byte-faithful.
#   foreign-repo          Cites paths and commit ids belonging to ANOTHER
#                         repository (Gas City); they never resolve here and are
#                         not supposed to.
#   pre-push-receipt      A per-bead pre-push receipt naming the files that bead
#                         touched. A later refactor moves or deletes them; the
#                         receipt still records what was true at push time.
#   orphaned-generator    KNOWN LIVE DEFECT, surfaced not fixed: the doc claims
#                         a generator that no longer exists in the tree. Fixing
#                         it means deciding the doc's fate, which belongs to a
#                         change that owns docs/evidence/**, not to this gate.

